{
  // A SEPARATE, dedicated Cloudflare Worker whose only job is to ping
  // bede-demo-api's /health on a schedule, so Render's free tier does not
  // spin it down between visitors.
  //
  // Deliberately NOT added to the repo-root wrangler.jsonc, which serves
  // agnusdei.ai itself. That config has no `main` field on purpose — its own
  // comment says so: "a Worker with only an `assets` block and no script
  // deploys as pure static hosting, no compute." Adding a scheduled()
  // handler there would mean introducing a script into the deployment of the
  // marketing site AND the demo, so a mistake in a keep-alive ping could
  // take down the front door. Here, the worst case is that the ping stops
  // and the backend goes back to cold-starting — exactly the situation this
  // replaces, and nothing a visitor to agnusdei.ai would ever notice.
  //
  // ── Schedule ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Every 5 minutes, 12:00-23:55 UTC. Two deliberate choices:
  //
  // 1. The WINDOW is unchanged from the GitHub Actions workflow this
  //    replaces (.github/workflows/keep-demo-warm.yml) and must stay that
  //    way. Render's free plan grants 750 instance-hours per MONTH across
  //    the whole workspace, and a 31-day month is 744 hours — so a keep-warm
  //    that actually worked around the clock would burn the entire
  //    allowance and get the service suspended for the rest of the month.
  //    That is strictly worse than cold starts. See docs/DEMO_HOSTING.md.
  //
  // 2. The CADENCE is 5 minutes rather than the workflow's 10. Render sleeps
  //    after 15 minutes idle, and Cloudflare states cron triggers may be
  //    delayed by a few minutes; 5 leaves roughly a 3x margin against that
  //    jitter instead of 1.5x. It costs nothing on either side — Workers'
  //    free tier is 100k requests/day against ~143 invocations here, and it
  //    adds no Render instance-hours at all, since the service is already
  //    continuously awake during the window either way.
  "name": "bede-keep-warm",
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-01",
  "triggers": {
    "crons": ["*/5 12-23 * * *"]
  },
  "vars": {
    // The demo backend's base URL — the same value as the repo's
    // VITE_DEMO_API_BASE variable, e.g.
    // "https://bede-demo-api-xxxx.onrender.com". Not a secret (it is baked
    // into the public demo bundle already), so it lives here rather than in
    // `wrangler secret`. Left empty on purpose: an unconfigured Worker logs
    // and does nothing rather than pinging some wrong host, mirroring how
    // the GitHub workflow handles an unset variable.
    "DEMO_API_BASE": ""
  },
  "observability": {
    // Without this, a silently failing ping looks identical to a working
    // one — the whole failure mode this Worker exists to fix.
    "enabled": true
  }
}
